<title>JAPAN: Advantest, Tokyo Elec surge to new 1997 highs.</title>
<headline>Advantest, Tokyo Elec surge to new 1997 highs.</headline>
<dateline>TOKYO 1997-05-29</dateline>
<text>
<p>Shares in Advantest Corp and Tokyo Electron Ltd surged to new highs for calendar 1997 early on Thursday morning.</p>
<p>Advantest, a semiconductor and semiconductor equipment maker, was up 220 yen at 7,450 at 0040 GMT and Tokyo Electron, an electronics trading firm, was up 140 yen at 5,360, after climbing as high as 5,370.  </p>
<p>&quot;The firms are viewed as laggards and are attracting buyers despite the fact that their earning forecasts are not spectacular,&quot; a trader at a second-tier brokerage said.</p>
</text>
